7. Final Result
Asymptotic analysis shows that Linear Search has linear growth, Binary Search has logarithmic growth, and Hash Table Search has constant average search growth when collisions are controlled.

For a student registration system containing more than one million records, Binary Search and Hash Table Search are generally more efficient than Linear Search for repeated searches.
- Linear Search: Suitable for small or unsorted datasets.
- Binary Search: Suitable for large, sorted datasets.
- Hash Table Search: Suitable for frequent registration-number searches when fast average lookup is required.
The choice of algorithm should consider not only searching time but also sorting cost, hash-table construction, memory usage and how frequently the data changes.
